00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:13.400
♪♪

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.167
Aww! Playing tonight,

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.934
we have the host of "The
Tonight Show," Mr. Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.367
-Oh, hi, everybody. Hello.

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:21.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:24.501
-And his opponent, the writer
of the "Comedians in Cars

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:28.434
Getting Coffee Book" available
now, Mr. Jerry Seinfeld.

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:31.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:35.434
And this is the first puppy
up for grabs.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:36.734
Gary Frick Jr.

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:39.067
[ Audience aws ]

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.901
Here's how the game works.

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:44.100
I'll be asking both of you
animal trivia questions.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.901
And if you answer correctly,

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:48.167
you win a Labrador
Retriever puppy.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.834
-It's a great game.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:53.634
-If you answer incorrectly,
your opponent gets the puppy.

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.300
So whoever has
the most puppies

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.367
at the end of the game
is guess what.

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:59.501
The Pup Quiz champion. Jerry.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:02.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.634
Jerry, you're our guest.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.000
So you'll answer
the first question.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.701
-Who is Gary Frick Jr.?
-Him right here.

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:12.100
-Gary Frick Jr. is
the name of the dog.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.033
And originally,
my dog's name was Gary.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.834
-Oh.
-That was the first
Gary Frick Jr.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.200
-Yeah, and it was a puppy
from this show.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.100
And it was a sketch we did.
And then at the end of the show,

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.968
I surprised my wife
with the puppy.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.334
-Oh, my God.
[ Audience aws ]

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.167
-Never surprise
your wife with a puppy.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.868
Terrible, terrible thing.
-Really?

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.601
-It's like getting someone
a job.

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:36.200
Honey, surprise.
You now work at 7-Eleven.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:39.701
-You're the assistant manager.
-That's great.

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:41.601
Don't cut that out.
Leave that joke in.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.767
That's great.

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:47.067
-I love that. Jerry Seinfeld's
like, "I loved it."

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.934
It makes my whole year.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.801
Made my whole year.
Alright, here we go.

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:54.133
-Alright, Jerry,
here's your question.

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:56.801
Where do wild turkeys sleep?

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:59.734
Is it A, in trees?

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:03.734
B, in tall grass?
Or C, in mud?

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:07.501
-Or D, who cares?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:10.834
The answer would be B,
in tall grass.

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:12.467
-This one's obvious.
-Tall grass.

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:13.634
That's what you're going to say?
-Yes.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.367
-Ooh! You're wrong.
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:17.667
The correct answer is trees.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.367
So, Jimmy,
you get Gary Frick Jr.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:21.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:24.300
-Hi, buddy.
-There you go.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.667
Trees.
-Hi.

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:27.834
-Next question is for you,
Jimmy.

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:30.133
Again, another turkey question.

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:33.634
Turkeys have three times
better blank than humans.

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:37.367
Smell, vision, or hearing?

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:42.667
-Well, they got to listen for,
like, knives sharpening.

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:45.801
-I'm going to say they have
better hearing than humans.

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:47.968
-Is that your final answer?
-Yes.

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:50.434
[ Buzzer ]
-That is incorrect. It's vision.

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:54.100
-I get a puppy!
-Jerry gets the next puppy.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.934
Adorable Mary Kennedy.
-Oh, there you go.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:03:00.167
-Hi. Hello.

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:01.934
-Does it make you happy?

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:03.868
-Yeah.
-Mary Kennedy.

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:06.367
-I got you. I got you.
-A puppy that makes you happy.

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.534
[ Barking ]
-Oh!

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.400
You know what that sound means.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.567
-That means...
-Time for Double Puppardy.

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:14.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:17.100
Where the questions are now
worth two puppies.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.901
-Oh!
-So it gets real spicy.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:22.200
Okay, Jerry, next question
for you.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.033
Group of turkeys
is called a what?

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:32.100
An A bale, B, parliament,
or C, rafter?

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.601
-This is supposed
to be a fun show.

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.267
These are like brain-breaking
questions.

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.300
-You're sitting in a La-Z-Boy
with a puppy.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.667
This is -- How more fun can you
get? I mean, come on.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.000
-A rafter.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.701
-Is that your final answer?
Correct!

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.567
-Wow. Look at you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:56.767
-Your new puppies are
Kyle McAdams and Lisa Armstrong.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:04:01.000
Oh, my gosh.
-Oh, I am puppy rich.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:05.667
Puppy rich. Puppies, puppy.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:08.200
-Okay, Next question
goes to Jimmy.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.734
-Feeling a little lonely
over there?

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.834
-We're bonding. We're bonding.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:16.634
-Male turkey droppings, right?
You know what that is.

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:19.734
Have a distinct shape
that looks like what?

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.133
A, a teardrop.

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:23.267
-Oh, gosh.
-B, an infinity sign.

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:24.968
-We just ate.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:27.501
-Or C, the letter J.

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:29.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.033
-That would be rude, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:34.267
-The infinity sign
is just stupid.

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:35.467
-That is just absolutely ridic--

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:38.067
-That takes a lot of effort.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.267
-But if I did see that,
I would be kind of amazed.

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:42.367
That would go on my Instagram,
probably.

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:45.267
-Yeah.
-Like a lowercase J can I ask?

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.567
-You said does it have
a little dot on the top?

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:51.167
That I don't know.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:52.868
-I'm going to say --
I don't know.

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:55.334
Turkey droppings. Teardrop.

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:57.234
-Teardrop? No!
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:58.667
The correct answer
was the letter J.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:04:59.934
-Yeah, letter J.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:02.834
-Jerry, say hello to
Roger Blaine and Ted Mooney.

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:08.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.934
Oh, my gosh.

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:13.968
-This is insane. This is insane.

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:16.234
Everyone's sniffing
each other's crotch.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:18.033
No one cares about anything.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:20.434
The rules have gone off.
This is off the rails.

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:23.100
-Oh!
-[ Barking ]

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.567
Wow.
You know what that sound means.

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:26.334
-What?
-Time for Final Puppardy.

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:28.334
-Okay. There you go.
-This question is for all

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.801
your opponent's puppies
and the game.

00:05:30.801 --> 00:05:32.734
-We have crushed him.

00:05:32.734 --> 00:05:35.100
[ Audience aws ]

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.567
-Come on! Come on now.

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:38.334
-Guys, get focused. Get focused.

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:40.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.667
-On average --
-Come on, Gary.

00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:43.467
Let's figure it out, buddy.
-On average,

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:47.467
how many turkeys does Butterball
sell per year?

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:49.067
That's a toughie.
-On average?

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:52.267
-On average.
10 seconds starting now!

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:54.267
-10 seconds. A year.
-A year?

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:55.901
-Yeah.
-I couldn't even tell you a day.

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:59.267
-Who cares?
-A year?

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:02.367
-Uh, how many turkeys
are there altogether?

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:03.701
[ Buzzer ]

00:06:03.701 --> 00:06:04.868
-Oh!

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:08.534
-Um, I'll say...

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.300
-This is -- If one of us
gets this right,

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.601
that would be insane.

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:13.100
I don't think we'd ever speak
to each other again.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.334
-I got it.
-Oh, you got it?

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:16.200
Alright, Jimmy,
what did you write down?

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.000
-I wrote 200,000.
-Ooh!

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.567
A year? Really?

00:06:20.567 --> 00:06:22.033
Okay, Jerry,
what did you write down?

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:24.634
-200,000.
-Wow!

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:28.000
-Dude!
-The answer...

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.734
...is 13 million!

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:31.934
You both win.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:34.367
[ Dinging ]

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:35.767
-We both wrote 200,000 turkeys.

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:38.300
-That is bizarre.
-That is bizarre.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:39.868
We bonded forever.

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:42.968
200,000 turkey-- Jerry Seinfeld,
everybody.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:45.367
All these adorable puppies.

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:46.901
Happy Thanksgiving.
Stick around.

00:06:46.901 --> 00:06:48.634
We'll be right back
with Adam Devine, everybody.

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:49.634
Come on back.

